{
  "version": 123,
  "released": "2026-08-06",
  "changelog": "v123: direct on-machine OpenAI-compatible models are now a first-class provider for the whole Lifehug Loop. Configure an Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp, or equivalent endpoint/model/timeout once and compile, classification, research, entity rosters, the Mirror, artifact revision, and connector dossiers all use it. Local routing is loopback-only and fail-closed by default: its transport bypasses proxy environment variables and rejects redirects, while an invalid, timed-out, malformed, or offline server returns to the existing agent-task path without silently sending private source material to a cloud fallback. The inherited OpenClaw loopback route now shares the same proxy-bypass and no-redirect boundary, validates its fixed localhost destination and port, and preserves explicit-versus-auto fallback semantics (#73). Configuration decode errors fail closed instead of erasing privacy choices; timeout, URL, header, construction, open, and read failures are typed and metadata-only; chat and readiness bodies are bounded for declared and chunked responses. `ai-status` explicitly performs a non-mutating readiness probe and reports provider and model, while viewer discovery remains network-free. Deliberate OpenClaw, Kimi, and Anthropic routes remain available, and the optional Anthropic SDK keeps v122's keyless/no-process-exit behavior. The shared router uses only Python's standard library and never logs prompts, source bodies, responses, or secrets.",
